      "description": "Watch Getafe vs Celta Vigo highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 7, 2026. The Coliseum played host to a gripping La Liga encounter between Getafe and Celta Vigo on September 7, 2026 . Both sides looked to assert their dominance in a clash defined by tactical discipline and high physical intensity. Satriano Breaks the Deadlock The match began with both teams testing each other's resolve, but it was the home side that struck first. In the 21st minute, Martin Satriano found the back of the net with a precise right-footed strike, rewarding Getafe for their early clinical edge. Despite the goal, Celta Vigo began to dominate possession, though they struggled to find a way through a stubborn defensive line. The first half ended with rising tensions, as Johan Mojica received a yellow card during stoppage time, leaving the hosts with a narrow lead at the break. Starfelt Equalizes as Momentum Shifts The second half saw a significant shift in dynamics. Celta Vigo returned with renewed vigor, and their persistence paid off in the 57th minute. Hugo Gonzalez delivered an accurate corner, allowing Carl Starfelt to power a header home and level the score. The situation worsened for Getafe just ten minutes later when Zaid Abner Romero was shown a second yellow card for a rough foul. Reduced to ten men, the home side was forced into a defensive shell for the remainder of the contest. Defensive Heroics Under Pressure With a man advantage, Celta Vigo ramped up the pressure, eventually finishing the match with a dominant 70% possession. David Soria was called into action to save a goal-bound header from Hugo Gonzalez , while Borja Iglesias saw an effort go wide. Despite the constant waves of attack from the visitors and several tactical substitutions aimed at breaking the deadlock, Getafe held firm. The match concluded in a stalemate after six minutes of stoppage time, characterized by desperate clearances and a resolute defensive display from the ten-man hosts."
